{
"opening": "This release focuses on stabilizing the command-line interface and introducing validation capabilities for version strings. We are addressing critical bugs in argument handling and adding new tools to verify version format compliance.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m07",
"text": "Calling the pysemver command without arguments must raise a SystemExit error instead of crashing with an AttributeError. Calling 'pysemver bump' without arguments must print the help text for the bump subcommand and exit successfully."
},
{
"id": "m12",
"text": "The internal regex used for parsing semantic versions must be updated to align with the official semver.org specification. Invalid version strings that previously passed validation should now be correctly identified as invalid."
},
{
"id": "m17",
"text": "The VersionInfo class must provide a static isvalid method that accepts a version string and returns a boolean indicating if it is valid. The pysemver CLI must include a new 'check' subcommand that utilizes this validation logic."
},
{
"id": "m19",
"text": "The pysemver CLI must support distinct functions for each subcommand, ensuring clear separation of logic for bump, check, and compare operations. The manpage documentation must explicitly define the return codes for these subcommands."
}
],
"closing": "Please ensure all public API changes are reflected in the documentation and that the CLI behaves predictably under edge cases."
}
